# ── ONE DATABASE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything for Shiv Hardware lives in the production deployment
# sensible-panther-176: bills, catalog, guarantees, toto, cash, attendance and
# the ledger books.
#
# WARNING: `npx convex dev` rewrites VITE_CONVEX_URL to the dev deployment.
# If it does, put it back to sensible-panther-176 before building — a build
# made with the dev URL ships an app that writes to the wrong database.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev deployment — used only by `npx convex dev` CLI (local dev / schema changes)
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:dapper-meadowlark-236 # team: harsh-agarwal, project: shiv-hardware-panel

# Production deployment — the app connects here at runtime
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://sensible-panther-176.convex.cloud
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://sensible-panther-176.convex.site
# Optional print server overrides. Leave absent to auto-use the same host as the panel on port 3333.
# VITE_PRINT_SERVER=http://<shop-computer-ip>:3333
# VITE_PRINT_SERVER_PORT=3333
VITE_CLOUD_API_URL=https://cloud-api-production-4953.up.railway.app
VITE_CLOUD_API_KEY=367cc5879d15d3493c49eb5e545008afdc12fec027f5297eb34f8c649fe9c992

# Where a printed card's QR sends the customer.
#
# Without this the QR encodes the print server, which answers only on the shop
# Wi-Fi — so a card scanned at home resolved to nothing. This is the public
# viewer: it reads the one card the QR names, and only for whoever holds the
# secret printed alongside it.
VITE_GUARANTEE_PUBLIC_URL=https://shiv-guarantee-viewer.vercel.app
